- crates/ai lands the plan's Controller trait verbatim: think(&mut self,
  view: &PlayerView, tick: Tick, out: &mut Vec<Command>) — perceive a
  fog-filtered view, decide, act by emitting commands (FD-7: ai depends
  only on fx + sim_api, structurally).
- ScriptedController: the Alpha opponent per plan §9.6 — scripted build
  order (workers -> depot -> barracks -> mixed army), idle-worker gather
  management (MoveState::Idle means no orders, so re-tasking can never
  cancel work in progress), attack waves on size + timer triggers with a
  seeded per-wave jitter, defense of the home radius, pending-train
  bookkeeping with expiry (the controller cannot see rejections: it
  verifies by sight through the next views), build attempts with
  candidate-spot consumption and cooldowns.
- AiPlan carries the public-knowledge facts a player reads off the screen
  (kind ids, costs, build times, starts, candidate build ground); live
  entities flow only through PlayerView (fog-honest).
- 15 unit tests: gather targeting, training gates (target/pending/
  cooldown/affordability/headroom), pending expiry + retirement, depot +
  barracks triggers, spot consumption on success and failure, round-robin
  army composition, defense cooldown + radius, wave transitions,
  per-tick sequence discipline, and controller determinism.
