The engine owns stepping the simulation (A-003), so it owns feeding the
controllers. AiMatchHost is the headless shape: per advance, every
controller thinks on its fog-filtered PlayerView of the tick being
applied (ascending slot order — determinism contract), all commands
feed the one step through the shared gate, and the log records exactly
what was fed (rejections included). Slots without a controller are
passive.

- alpha_controller/alpha_plan derive the scripted opponent's config
  from the loaded content by capability shape: production lists decide
  the roster (the barracks list is the army, the other producer trains
  workers), supply is the cheapest non-CC population structure, the
  node kind carries a Resource body; costs map through the same Ore
  seam the content bundle uses; starts come from the map.
- build_spots: deterministic ring scan (Chebyshev rings, row-major,
  nearest-first) around each start — footprint-fitting, buildable,
  clear of t0 static claims, and one tile off node doorsteps (the M5
  chokepoint lesson). Map knowledge, not fog-protected state (A-061).
- controller RNG seeds derive from the match seed mixed by slot.
- 7 engine tests: fog-filtered views feed the gate, the log records
  rejections verbatim, ascending controller order, outside-slot refusal
  (should-panic), log-only re-simulation equality (FD-1), and the spot
  scan's legality + nearest-first ordering.
