  M1 scripted match and its pinned hash 0x9d5ba9b565060336 unchanged)
  and --content (default ./content). --p1 ai --p2 ai runs the Alpha
  content with two scripted opponents through the engine's hosting;
  idle slots watch. The printout gains the per-player evidence line
  (deliveries, trained, built, hits, deaths) — the machine-visible
  'match result' until match rules land in M8.
- ai_match: the match driver (setup from map starts, controllers via
  alpha_controller, checkpoints + forced final, replay record with the
  full fed log) and the per-player summary built from the event stream
  (site owners mapped through ConstructionStarted's builder — sites
  spawn without Spawned events).
- ScriptedController build verification switched from spot-proximity to
  count-of-own-entities-of-that-kind: the 3-tile sight tolerance gave
  false successes on adjacent candidate spots, cycling placements
  every 2 ticks. The count is pure view arithmetic and exact.
- replay-verify resolves the world by content identity: the demo world,
  then the content directory — a precise error lists all candidates'
  hashes. AI replays verify PASS (41+ checkpoints reproduced from the
  log alone); demo replays unchanged.
- tools -> engine edge added to the law's allow-list (A-003-style
  amendment, A-063): the headless runner hosts controllers through the
  same engine-owned hosting the client will use in M8 — one loop, not
  a second copy. The architecture-law test stays green.
