- A5 (structural): the ai manifest depends on exactly fx + sim_api
  (re-asserted in-suite, belt to the law's braces); the sim and sim_api
  sources never reference the ai crate — no AI-specific entry point
  exists to find.
- A5 (behavioral): the ledger identity over the flagship AI match —
  final Ore == starting + deliveries (data-defined carry per trip) -
  accepted Train/Build costs at the data-defined prices, per player;
  every entity beyond the starting forces traces to an accepted Train or
  Build minus deaths; the scripted opponent never cancels (no refunds
  to account); both sides fought. The AI pays the player prices.
- A11 (deterministic): a 20-pair mirrored battery over the real content
  — player 0 (labeled Human) and player 1 (labeled Ai) issue
  structurally identical commands; every pair validates identically,
  and the battery exercises every rejection class reachable at match
  start. Controller labels never change outcomes (the same battery
  under Human/Human and Ai/Ai reproduces the identical outcome map) —
  labels are recorded match identity, not behavior.
- A11 (property): a proptest fuzz generating random mirrored commands
  (side-relative entity slots, 180-degree-mirrored positions with
  footprint-aware Build placement, random kinds/indices) over fresh
  matches — every generated pair validates identically.
- Completion: three seeded 2400-tick matches run their full budget
  under the debug A12 checker with real economies, infrastructure, and
  armies; each seeded run is bit-identical (log + checkpoints + final
  hash); seeds diverge (pre-wave logs may legitimately match — the
  script's only randomness is the wave jitter — but the hashed RNG
  state still separates the states).
- Golden: the flagship 7200-tick match pins its tick-0 and final hashes
  (0x61613bca16b8f00e, 0x679f4713114765c9).
- A2 over an AI-driven log: the flagship record validates, round-trips
  the codec, and re-simulates — controllers absent — to every
  checkpoint and the final hash. FD-1: the log is the match.
